  "Question": "While eating out, Mike and Joe each tipped their server \\(\\$2.\\) Mike tipped \\(10\\%\\) of his bill and Joe tipped \\(20\\%\\) of his bill. What was the difference, in dollars, between their bills?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(10\\)",
    "E": "\\(20\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Mike's \\(10\\%\\) tip is \\(\\frac1{10}\\) of his bill. His \\(2\\)-dollar tip is therefore one of ten equal parts of the bill, so his bill was \\(10\\cdot2=20\\) dollars.\n\nJoe's \\(20\\%\\) tip is \\(\\frac15\\) of his bill. His bill was therefore \\(5\\cdot2=10\\) dollars.\n\nThe difference between their bills was \\(20-10=10\\) dollars, choice D.",
